From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:44:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vfio/pci: add x-inject-internal-error to test crash handling

EVE saves a guest core when a VM stops in the internal-error run state,
which is where a KVM_RUN failure, such as a fault on a disabled
passthrough BAR, leaves it. Reaching that state on demand would otherwise
take the hardware race, so add a QMP command that stops the VM there
directly.

The command exists only in builds with CONFIG_EVE_CRASH_INJECTOR defined.
Its QAPI definition carries the same condition, so other builds have
neither the code nor the command. EVE's tools/qemu/inject-crash.sh sends
it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [EVE debug aid]
Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 hw/vfio/pci.c  | 14 ++++++++++++++
 qapi/vfio.json | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/vfio/pci.c b/hw/vfio/pci.c
index 428ab2f..3d94be3 100644
--- a/hw/vfio/pci.c
+++ b/hw/vfio/pci.c
@@ -4148,6 +4148,20 @@ static const TypeInfo vfio_pci_nohotplug_info = {
     .class_init = vfio_pci_nohotplug_class_init,
 };
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_EVE_CRASH_INJECTOR
+#include "qapi/qapi-commands-vfio.h"
+
+/*
+ * Stop the VM in the internal-error run state, as a KVM_RUN failure would,
+ * so that crash handling can be tested without reproducing a real fault.
+ * Debug builds only; see qapi/vfio.json.
+ */
+void qmp_x_inject_internal_error(Error **errp)
+{
+    vm_stop(RUN_STATE_INTERNAL_ERROR);
+}
+#endif
+
 static void register_vfio_pci_dev_type(void)
 {
     /*
diff --git a/qapi/vfio.json b/qapi/vfio.json
index 17b6046..81acefe 100644
--- a/qapi/vfio.json
+++ b/qapi/vfio.json
@@ -75,3 +75,23 @@
       'qom-path': 'str',
       'device-state': 'QapiVfioMigrationState'
   } }
+
+##
+# @x-inject-internal-error:
+#
+# Stop the VM in the internal-error run state, as a KVM_RUN failure
+# would, so that crash handling can be tested on demand.  Only built
+# with CONFIG_EVE_CRASH_INJECTOR defined.
+#
+# Features:
+#
+# @unstable: This command is meant for testing.
+#
+# .. qmp-example::
+#
+#     -> { "execute": "x-inject-internal-error" }
+#     <- { "return": {} }
+##
+{ 'command': 'x-inject-internal-error',
+  'features': [ 'unstable' ],
+  'if': 'CONFIG_EVE_CRASH_INJECTOR' }
